        "comments": [
          {
            "id": "PRRC_kwDOVpFduc8AAAABGUSGRA",
            "database_id": 4718888516,
            "body": "<!-- devin-review-comment {\"id\": \"BUG_pr-review-job-1be65645956d480f8767b3dabc07b228_0001\", \"file_path\": \"cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo\", \"start_line\": 936, \"end_line\": 939, \"side\": \"RIGHT\", \"based_on_repo_rules\": false, \"kind\": \"bug\"} -->\n\n🟡 **Valid updates rejected after typed literals**\n\nWith `name'…'` followed by a continuation ending in one backslash, `maskStringFor` skips the closing quote. [backslashEscapes](https://github.com/gosuda/spira/blob/82ce092dd0799ee6f644262d3c724c587350633a/cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo#L981-L989 \"cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo:981-989\") mistakes the type name’s final `e` for an escape prefix. An update that names `version` only in the following assignment then fails generation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Learn more</summary>\n\nPostgreSQL permits a type name immediately before a string literal and parses `name'…'` as a typed literal, not an escape string. [backslashEscapes](https://github.com/gosuda/spira/blob/82ce092dd0799ee6f644262d3c724c587350633a/cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo#L981-L989 \"cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo:981-989\") checks only the byte before the opening quote. Propagating that result to a continuation makes [maskQuotedFor](https://github.com/gosuda/spira/blob/82ce092dd0799ee6f644262d3c724c587350633a/cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo#L991-L1009 \"cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo:991-1009\") skip a real closing quote and blank the following assignment. [refuseVersionedWrite](https://github.com/gosuda/spira/blob/82ce092dd0799ee6f644262d3c724c587350633a/cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo#L894-L905 \"cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/model.lgo:894-905\") then reports that the statement writes the table without `version`.\n\n**Example:** Use `UPDATE items SET name = name'first '` followed on the next line by `'last\\', version = version + 1 WHERE id = 1;`. The PostgreSQL parser returns a cast to `name` and a separate assignment to `version`. A focused scanner trace gives `FAIL: writes versioned table items without version` with the current prefix check and `PASS: version visible` with a token-boundary check.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Identify a standalone PostgreSQL `E` prefix before inheriting its escape mode across continuation segments. Add the compact typed-literal example to [TestPostgresContinuedEscapeStrings](https://github.com/gosuda/spira/blob/82ce092dd0799ee6f644262d3c724c587350633a/cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/continued_escape_test.lgo#L18-L38 \"cmd/sqlc-gen-spira/continued_escape_test.lgo:18-38\") alongside the existing genuine `E'…'` cases, and run the same generator test before and after the repair with the LoGOs toolchain.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n<a href=\"https://app.devin.ai/review/gosuda/spira/pull/47\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->\n\n---\n*Was this helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to provide feedback.*",
